{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"The expression for $g(x)$ includes $\\cos(x)$.\n\nRemember that the derivative of $\\cos(x)$ is $-\\sin(x)$.\n\nPut another way, $\\dfrac{d}{dx}[\\cos(x)]=-\\sin(x)$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"$\\begin{align}\ng'(x)\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}[-2\\cos(x)+3x^3]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-2\\dfrac{d}{dx}[\\cos(x)]+3\\dfrac{d}{dx}(x^3)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-2(-\\sin(x))+3\\cdot3x^2\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=2\\sin(x)+9x^2\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"In conclusion,\n\n$g'(x)=2\\sin(x)+9x^2$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"Let $g(x)=-2\\cos(x)+3x^3$.\n\n$g'(x)=$ [[☃ expression 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"expression 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"answerForms":[{"considered":"correct","form":false,"key":0,"simplify":false,"value":"2\\sin\\left(x\\right)+9x^2"}],"buttonSets":["basic","trig","prealgebra"],"functions":["f","g","h"],"times":false},"static":false,"type":"expression","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
